# Normalize line endings on commit, and check out with the platform
# default. Text files are stored in the repository with LF endings, so
# a checkout on Windows (CRLF) and a checkout on macOS/Linux (LF)
# produce the same content, and a diff never shows a whole file as
# changed just because of line endings.
#
# This matters for this project in practice: the Windows verification
# session ran against a source tree extracted from a GitHub zip, which
# arrives with CRLF. Without this file, every one of those files
# showed up as modified.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by the eol machinery.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.msi binary
*.dmg binary
*.deb binary
*.rpm binary
*.appimage binary

# Lockfiles and generated files are still text — they only need the
# same LF normalization, so `text=auto eol=lf` is kept rather than
# opting them out of the eol machinery. Marking them `-text` would
# make every line a diff on a CRLF checkout.
misedeck/package-lock.json text eol=lf
misedeck/src-tauri/Cargo.lock text eol=lf
